@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, word wrap, crop, apply markup, or replace emoji codes. Output is written as plain text, so ``[bold]`` and ``:smiley:`` are written literally.
+
+It does apply highlighting and a basic ``style``. The ``highlight`` argument defaults to ``True``, which forces highlighting even if the Console was created with highlighting disabled. Pass ``highlight=None`` to use the Console default, or ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off.
+
+
